g~" class=3D"css-sdwaa1" style=3D"color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-decoration:und=
erline;text-decoration:underline">Stolen Revolution</a><span>=E2=80=9D is i=
n part about why the economic promises of the 1979 revolution went unfulfil=
led.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;m=
argin:0 0 15px"><span>This is just not a regime that has prioritized econom=
ic growth, Yeganeh told me.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px geo=
rgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>During the revolution to overt=
hrow the shah, Ruhollah Khomeini, who would become Iran=E2=80=99s first sup=
reme leader, and other revolutionaries made gestures at the idea of improvi=
ng people=E2=80=99s material lives. They talked about free electricity for =
the poor and more housing; they used Marxism-inflected language, talking ab=
out the oppressors and the oppressed.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17p=
x/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Then the revolution =
succeeded and, as early as September of 1979, Khomeini made his true priori=
ties clear:</span></p><p style=3D"font:17px/25px georgia,serif;margin:0 50p=
x 15px;color:#666" class=3D"css-14jlz04"><span>=E2=80=9CNo wise person can =
imagine that we sacrificed our blood so that melons would become cheap! [Th=
at] we gave our youth so that housing would become affordable =E2=80=A6 It =
is for Islam that a person can give up his life. Our saints also gave up th=
eir lives for Islam, not for economics. Economics is not worthy of this.=E2=
=80=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333=
;margin:20px 0 15px"><span>This is a regime that cares about ideology, Yega=
neh said. For all that=E2=80=99s changed since Khomeini, it still retains t=
hat in its DNA.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;c=
olor:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Occasionally, the regime is forced to face=
 the reality that things have gotten so dire its survival is at stake. That=
=E2=80=99s what brought them to the table to negotiate a nuclear deal in 20=
15, and the economy is worse today, she said.</span></p><p style=3D"font:no=
rmal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The protests=
 that brought thousands into the streets in January were driven by economic=
s. That=E2=80=99s partly why there is a faction within Iran that does want =
to reach a deal with the U.S.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px g=
eorgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>But there=E2=80=99s another =
faction that remains convinced that, in the current standoff, the U.S. will=
 blink first.</span></p><table border=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"0" cellspacing=
